      "text": "### Rhizobium Symbiosis"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-LEGUMES.md#016",
      "path": [
        "02-LEGUMES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:food-plants:02-legumes, git-history:food-plants:02-legumes]",
        "canonical_path": "food-plants/02-LEGUMES.md",
        "concepts": "[legumes]",
        "current_path": "food-plants/02-LEGUMES.md",
        "id": "maxim:food-plants:legumes",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "food-plants",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[legumes]",
        "section": "food-plants",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Legumes - Nitrogen Fixation and Protein Architecture",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nLEGUME ROOT NODULE FORMATION\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n1. Legume root exudes flavonoids (signal molecules)\n       │\n       ▼\n2. Rhizobium bacteria respond → produce Nod factors (lipochitooligosaccharides)\n       │\n       ▼\n3. Root hair curls around bacteria → infection thread forms\n       │\n       ▼\n4. Bacteria enter root cortex cells → multiply\n       │\n       ▼\n5. Bacteria differentiate into BACTEROIDS (nitrogen-fixing form)\n       │\n       ▼\n6. NODULE forms: specialized organ, pink/red when active\n       │\n       ▼\n7. Plant provides: photosynthate (sucrose) for bacterial energy\n   Bacteria provide: NH₃ for plant protein synthesis"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-LEGUMES.md#017",
      "path": [
        "02-LEGUMES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:food-plants:02-legumes, git-history:food-plants:02-legumes]",
        "canonical_path": "food-plants/02-LEGUMES.md",
        "concepts": "[legumes]",
        "current_path": "food-plants/02-LEGUMES.md",
        "id": "maxim:food-plants:legumes",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "food-plants",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[legumes]",
        "section": "food-plants",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Legumes - Nitrogen Fixation and Protein Architecture",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "LEGHEMOGLOBIN: pink/red color of active nodule\n  - Plant-derived globin protein + iron-heme cofactor\n  - Binds O₂ with high affinity (similar to hemoglobin)\n  - Maintains very low [O₂] around bacteroids while allowing respiration\n  - Without it: nitrogenase destroyed, no N₂ fixation\n  - Globin proteins are ancient and widespread; leghemoglobin is a plant-bacterial\n    symbiosis adaptation, not an animal-gene import.\n```"
    }
